<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Instructions of the Year XIII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Instructions of the Year XIII were the directions given in April 1813 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">José Gervasio Artigas</a> and a congress of the Eastern Province to its deputies at the assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>. They called for independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, a republican government, a federal union of the provinces and a capital outside Buenos Aires. Buenos Aires refused to seat the deputies, and the document became a founding text of Uruguayan federalism.</p></div>
